{# Theme toggle — a two-segment control, not a switch. With exactly two
   identities a segmented control states what the alternative IS, where a single
   cycling button would hide it behind a guess.

   `data-theme-option` is the contract with assets/vue/fx/theme.ts;
   `data-theme-chrome` carries Theme::browserColor() so that module never has to
   duplicate the palette. Accessible names are the identity names themselves
   (proper nouns, identical in all 21 locales); only the group label is
   translated, and `aria-pressed` carries the state.

   The header renders this twice — inline in the right cluster from `sm` up, and
   inside the preferences popover below it, where the bar has no room left. Only
   one is ever displayed, and the module keeps every instance in sync, so the two
   never disagree.

   Without JavaScript the control is inert. That is deliberate: the identity is
   presentation, the server-rendered one is complete, and nothing here gates
   content. Params: class. #}
{% set currentTheme = app_theme.current %}
<div class="theme-toggle {{ class|default('') }}" role="group"
     aria-label="{{ 'header.theme.label'|trans }}">
  {% for theme in app_theme.options %}
    <button type="button"
            class="theme-toggle__option"
            data-theme-option="{{ theme.value }}"
            data-theme-chrome="{{ theme.browserColor }}"
            aria-pressed="{{ theme.value == currentTheme.value ? 'true' : 'false' }}"
            title="{{ theme.label }}">
      {% include 'components/ui/_theme_crest.html.twig' with { theme: theme.value } only %}
      <span class="sr-only">{{ theme.label }}</span>
    </button>
  {% endfor %}
</div>
